    755          /**
    756           *  @brief     Motor Control Loop for 3-Phase motors (DD,BPM,CIM).
    757           *  @details   Motor control loop routine for 3-Phase motors :
    758           *             - d axis: rotor flux position
    759           *             - q axis: rotor flux quadrature axis
    760           *
    761           *             This routine is composed by six parts:
    762           *             - Input processing: tachometer signal processing
    763           *                                 motor speed reference absolute value
    764           *                                 motor phase currents swapping in order to work with a positive speed reference.
    765           *                                 dc voltage filtering
    766           *
    767           *             - Observer:		   rotor flux speed estimation
    768           *             					   flux position estimation (FOC: rotor flux, DTC: stator flux)
    769           *
    770           *             - Speed Controller: speed PI execution
    771           *								   torque reference generation
    772           *
    773           *             - Dq Reference Gen: Mtpa
    774           *                                 Flux Weaking
    775           *             					   d-reference generation (FOC: current Id, DTC: flux reference)
    776           *             					   q reference generation (FOC: current Id, DTC: torque reference)
    777           *								   torque reference generation
    778           *
    779           *             - Dq Controller:   DQ PI execution (FOC: current PI, DTC: flux/torque PI)
    780           *								  alpha-beta voltage reference generation
    781           *
    782           *             - Pwm:   		  DC voltage compensation
    783           *             					  Deadtime compensation
    784           *             					  PWM Duties generation
    785           *  @param[in]     
    786           *  @param[out]     
    787           *  @param[in]
    788           *  @return        
    789           */

